From 50a611b148560b8e053460ab286140290bc299a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Alman <haven@thehavennet.org.uk>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:07:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(host/v2): keep tool-call pairing when v2 context
 messages carry no id

The v2 host hands session.hook('context') messages with no `id`, so
onV2ContextEvent paired transformed v1 views back by position. The v1
chain changes the view count (materializeSystemGuidanceInPlace converts a
mid-history system entry into a re-homed carrier; verdict inserts), so
later views landed on the wrong message and the trailing one was dropped,
orphaning a tool_result the provider rejects. writeBackTextParts also
moved assistant preamble text after its tool call.

Pair views by object identity (then id, then position for rebuilt views
only), never drop a message carrying non-text parts, rebuild in host
order, and write text back in position.

Closes #3423
