From 3f340d633bb24160e57b874f20c6928562e5f402 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <a@b.c>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:21:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(host/v2): pair context views by an origin stamp
 instead of position

Review follow-up for #3424. The positional fallback could not tell a structuredClone-rebuilt view from a chain-inserted one, so after the guardrails retry rollback an id-less insert (full-auto verdict) could take a later same-role message's text slot. Views now carry a string origin index (info.swarmV2Origin) that survives structuredClone and the carrier materialization spread; pairing is identity, then id, then the stamp (integer, in range, same role, first claim wins), and unstamped chain inserts are dropped. The positional fallback is removed.

Also: a carrier-consumed source is no longer retained just because it has non-text parts (guidance was delivered twice); non-array content is left untouched instead of being split into characters; event.messages is refilled with a loop instead of a spread push. Tests now pin the retention branch, the stamp mechanics, rollback plus insert, and consumed carrier sources, and clean up their temp dirs. The release note and hook inventory describe the dropped id-less inserts and the pairing contract.

Refs #3423

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
